  "research_id": "insurance-reinsurance",
  "title": "Insurance and Reinsurance",
  "question": "Which sovereign and supervisory authorities define the insurance constitution, how do insurer balance sheets transmit monetary and capital-market policy, who transfers or retains risk, and which private or public balance sheet ultimately pays or recoups a covered loss?",
  "bluf": "Big insurance is a distributed public-private balance-sheet constitution. Sovereign law and state legal-entity supervision form the base; NAIC coordination, lead-state tools, federal functional perimeters, IAIS standards and foreign supervisors add group and system windows without creating one insurance ministry. Across borders, global standards, domestic implementation, covered agreements, equivalence decisions, cooperation arrangements, group colleges, reserve-credit rules and resolution powers are distinct controls; none turns a group into one freely transferable balance sheet. At year-end 2025, FIO reported $9.902 trillion of life-sector assets and $3.223 trillion of property/casualty assets, making insurers major buyers of bonds, mortgages, structured assets and private credit. Monetary conditions, capital treatment, reinsurance and FHLBank liquidity can therefore transmit through insurer portfolios into borrower financing and market stress. Liquidity is a timed-cash problem distinct from solvency, while asset risk reaches statutory capital through a separate ratings, designation, accounting and RBC chain. Ownership adds another chain: proposed control, approval, closing, board governance, affiliate dealings, fees, dividends and support remain legally distinct, and owning insurer shares does not confer ownership of insurer assets. Pension risk transfer changes the obligor only through the chosen transaction, contract and distribution state; it also moves protection from the PBGC plan perimeter toward state-regulated annuity and guaranty frameworks. PMI, title, financial guaranty and surety can gate credit and execution before loss but do not erase the underlying duty. Compulsory financial responsibility starts above the policy by defining the activity, acceptable security, public proof and lapse consequence. Economic, statutory, investor and tax measurements remain distinct from capital and cash. Price-Anderson, commercial-space excess claims, FAA war-risk insurance and SAFETY Act protections use different private/public liability structures. Domestic insurer failure ordinarily passes through state receivership, bounded guaranty protection, assessments and estate recovery rather than ordinary chapter 7. Policy, claim, filing, custody and collateral records remain operational control objects: restoration is not reconciliation, and reconciliation is not completed remedy. Product-line and retail records are downstream evidence of this sovereign, supervisory, capital, ownership, risk-transfer, operational and public-loss machine.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-10-01T16:00:00-04:00",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "The maintained U.S. carrier/treaty answer remains sourced through July 12, 2026. The bounded Japan comparison is refreshed through September 15 02:55 JST. The top-down monetary/government control map and the actuarial, life/annuity, homeowners, health, commercial, cross-border, liquidity, capital, ownership, pension, credit, operations, employment, public-pool, crop, alternative-capital, trade/political-risk, compulsory-cover, accounting/tax, federal-indemnity and domestic-failure extensions use sources checked October 1. The October 1 CRP meeting and October 7 interconnectedness discussion remained future clocks. The extensions are not fresh company, treaty, plan, pool, crop-policy, transaction, state-market, security, tax-return, receivership or service-contract censuses.",
  "use_note": "Start with the constitutional thesis, then the October 1 top-down map and interactive hub. Route to the lens whose legal trigger and balance sheet fit the question: employment status, public-pool membership, crop policy, ILS contract, trade receivable or political-risk guarantee are not interchangeable. Then move into the dated evidence owner. The thesis is an interpretation, not a substitute for policy, trigger, claim, payment or recovery records. The carrier/treaty core remains a July 12 snapshot; the later extensions do not refresh every exposure, policy, pool, security, treaty, transaction, claim, recovery or paid loss.",
  "library_state": "current",
